# Mockito — testing in isolation

## Mocks — fakes you program

```java
PaymentGateway gw = mock(PaymentGateway.class);
when(gw.charge(100)).thenReturn(Result.APPROVED);   // stub

OrderService svc = new OrderService(gw);            // inject the fake
svc.placeOrder(order);                              // tests ONLY OrderService
```

No bank, no network — instant + deterministic. Script failure too: `.thenThrow(new TimeoutException())`.

## Verify interactions

```java
verify(gw).charge(100);               // must have charged 100
verify(emailer, never()).send(any()); // must NOT email on failure
```

## Mindset

- **Mock at boundaries** — DB, network, clock — not your own value objects
- **Don't over-mock** — verifying implementation, not behavior, breaks on every refactor

## The whole concept

`main` + JVM → objects → modern types → collections → generics → functional → streams → errors & I/O → concurrency → **runtime, build, test**. Java you can **ship and trust**.
